@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
   <div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need form 721 if I have not sold anything?</summary><p>Possibly. The initial obligation depends on foreign custody and a combined value above €50,000 at 31 December, not on selling coins or withdrawing money.</p></details><details><summary>Is the €50,000 threshold separate for each platform?</summary><p>No. Add together all foreign-held virtual currencies within the reporting obligation, even if several custodians hold them. If the combined limit is exceeded, all those currencies are reported.</p></details><details><summary>Do coins in my own wallet count?</summary><p>No, if you control the private keys and no third party holds them in custody for you. The Tax Agency says actual custody matters, whether the wallet is hot or cold.</p></details><details><summary>Does selling everything remove the obligation in later years?</summary><p>Not necessarily. If selling means you stop being the holder, authorised person or beneficiary of those coins, you report the balances at the date that status ended and, in that case, the regulation requires the return to be filed in any event (article 42 quater, sections 4 and 6). We check each case.</p></details></div>
